  "reconstructibility": 2,
  "reason": "The records collectively provide the main ingredients of the later result. R1 and R13 establish indentation-derived properties and temperature-dependent friction/wear in HEA coatings, including increasing friction and wear at elevated temperature. R2-R6 document temperature-driven changes in dislocation, slip, twinning, creep, and recrystallization mechanisms. Most importantly, R11 supplies molecular-dynamics evidence for partial-dislocation friction and coupled FCC-HCP transformation in a closely related FCC CoNiCrFeMn nanosystem, while R14 explicitly examines elevated-temperature order-disorder transitions in HEAs. Thus, although no single record gives the exact FeNiCrCoCu-on-Cu geometry, temperature schedule, or sharp 900 K threshold, an expert could plausibly combine established temperature-dependent coating tribology with atomistic HEA deformation and order-disorder concepts to propose the later intervention and mechanism."
